      "content": "If the patterns resemble mathematical interference, they might be leveraging principles of visual rhythm and frequency to influence perception, bordering on the area of visual pattern recognition mechanics. While definitive proof is complex, highly structured, non-random patterns can impact alertness and cognitive load. This targeted visual stimulus might be designed to create a momentary cognitive dissonance or surge of focused attention, which the brand can then associate with the purchase decision.",
